                                        "glosses": [
                                            "The process of reverse-engineering the encryption used by cryptocurrency in order to generate cryptocurrency."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "11dc0d2f-df51-498a-a7b2-4349eb6173b7",
                                                "sense_id": "c1e06399-3106-3f09-b886-8d7be3c31863",
                                                "text": "It’s almost as if cryptomining were designed to break graphics cards – miners usually run their graphics cards for 24 hours, and the process creates a lot of heat."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "6048316a-99a7-45d0-9202-ca34f089979e",
                                                "sense_id": "c1e06399-3106-3f09-b886-8d7be3c31863",
                                                "text": "Demin warned that more companies could face malicious software capable of cryptomining. Of late, a number of businesses were caught running cryptomining code on their websites to secretly generate digital currencies as an alternative to online advertising."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "cd387e28-7e08-4ae6-abd8-c09bdf78c30d",
                                                "sense_id": "c1e06399-3106-3f09-b886-8d7be3c31863",
                                                "text": "One currency that is actively mined through cryptomining malware is Monero."
                                            }
